From: pi-bmc rpi5-uefi build <pi-bmc@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] PlatformBm: return the boot option number, not the list index

PlatformRegisterBootOption () returns the INDEX of the option in the
BootOrder-sorted load option array (EfiBootManagerFindLoadOption's
return, or BootOptionCount after an append).  Its caller
PlatformRegisterOptionsAndKeys () then passes that value to
EfiBootManagerAddKeyOptionVariable () as the Boot#### option NUMBER for
the F1-to-Shell hotkey.

On a factory-fresh variable store the two happen to coincide (the shell
is Boot0000 sitting at index 0), so the bug is invisible.  As soon as
BootOrder/Boot#### variables survive from earlier boots (here: restored
from the BMC-emulated EEPROM by EepromVarStoreDxe before BDS runs) the
index and the number diverge, Boot%04x(index) does not exist, and
EfiBootManagerAddKeyOptionVariable returns EFI_NOT_FOUND, tripping

  ASSERT [BdsDxe] PlatformBm.c(500): Status == RETURN_SUCCESS ||
                                     Status == RETURN_ALREADY_STARTED

which dead-loops DEBUG builds during BDS.

Return the real option number instead: for an existing match, the
OptionNumber of the matched entry; for a fresh registration, the number
EfiBootManagerAddLoadOptionVariable assigned into NewOption.
---
 .../Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBm.c   | 12 +++++++++---
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBm.c	2026-08-10 13:45:16.918121287 -0500
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBm.c	2026-08-10 13:45:33.318801174 -0500
@@ -353,6 +353,7 @@
 {
   EFI_STATUS                        Status;
   INTN                              OptionIndex;
+  INTN                              OptionNumber;
   EFI_BOOT_MANAGER_LOAD_OPTION      NewOption;
   EFI_BOOT_MANAGER_LOAD_OPTION      *BootOptions;
   UINTN                             BootOptionCount;
@@ -376,13 +377,21 @@
   if (OptionIndex == -1) {
     Status = EfiBootManagerAddLoadOptionVariable (&NewOption, MAX_UINTN);
     ASSERT_EFI_ERROR (Status);
-    OptionIndex = BootOptionCount;
+    //
+    // Callers hand the return value to EfiBootManagerAddKeyOptionVariable
+    // as a Boot#### NUMBER, so return the number assigned by
+    // EfiBootManagerAddLoadOptionVariable - not the list index, which only
+    // matches the number on a factory-fresh variable store.
+    //
+    OptionNumber = EFI_ERROR (Status) ? -1 : (INTN)NewOption.OptionNumber;
+  } else {
+    OptionNumber = (INTN)BootOptions[OptionIndex].OptionNumber;
   }
 
   EfiBootManagerFreeLoadOption (&NewOption);
   EfiBootManagerFreeLoadOptions (BootOptions, BootOptionCount);
 
-  return OptionIndex;
+  return OptionNumber;
 }
 
 STATIC
